  message: "THIS ITEM PARTLY DUPLICATES WORK ALREADY FILED, and I should have found it\nbefore filing. Recording the overlap rather than leaving three parallel items.\n\nI searched the tracker for this before filing and searched only TITLES from a\ncapped `list`, which found nothing. Searching every item BODY (1,917 items)\nfinds the stream immediately:\n\n  WI-kazas  P1 todo_soft  MEAS-1: baseline full-run wall-clock. THE GATE.\n  WI-zagij  P2 todo_hard  INC-2: package/workspace-scoped re-analysis.\n  WI-madut  P3 todo_soft  INC-1: per-file memoization on git blob sha.\n  WI-zopis  P4 needs_human_review  persist CFG/DDG as a source-derived sidecar.\n  WI-rukaz  P3 todo_hard  a ~14.6k-file Java repo at >60 min, bottleneck\n                          unlocated -- the plausible \"tens of minutes\" cell.\n\nBoth fix candidates I wrote into this item's description were already filed, with\nbetter-developed hazard analysis than mine: WI-madut names the per-file purity\naudit, the complete-key silent-stale-hit failure mode, the determinism\nprecondition, and the linkers as an irreducible remainder. All three were\nDEFERRED pending MEAS-1 \"proving full-run latency actually hurts. Do NOT build\nuntil the number demands it.\"\n\nSO WHAT THIS ITEM IS ACTUALLY FOR: it is the measurement that satisfied that\ngate, taken from the dogfooding loop rather than from the target-repo spread\nMEAS-1 asked for. The numbers now live on WI-kazas (latency table + band\nverdict), WI-zagij (ungated, P3 -> P2), and WI-madut (why it stays deferred).\nThe distinct contribution not covered by any of them is the PER-EDIT framing:\nMEAS-1's decision rule prices a cold run as a one-off a user waits through,\nwhile the local loop pays it on every invocation, which is what makes 8.2\nminutes read as 97% of the cycle instead of a tolerable wait.\n\nRETAINED, NOT DELETED, for two reasons: deletion needs human authority, and the\nper-edit finding plus the smart-test phase table are worth an address. Status ->\ndone, since the measurement is complete and the fix work belongs on the items\nabove. If the owner would rather have this folded away entirely, it is a\n`tracker delete` away and nothing depends on it.\n\nNEXT MEASUREMENT, cheap and decisive for both fix items: the analysis-vs-linking\nsplit of one cold run. If linking dominates the 489 s then neither package\nscoping nor per-file memoization helps much and the target is the linker stage.\nThe per-pass timers in AnalysisRun already carry the data."  # d73c
